{{ ansible_managed | comment }}
# Homepage service layout — auto-generated by docker_services post-deploy hook.
# Source of truth: group_vars/vps.yml docker_services list + this template
# (homepage moved to the VPS per HD-180; implemented HD-183).
# See docs/interfaces.md for the 6-tier interface model.
#
# HD-316: family dashboard split on kogler.si / home.kogler.si.
#   - Family groups (Photos/Files/Docs/Chat/Git/AI/Tools/Accounts): tile the
#     LIVE, publicly-routed apps. Health dots = Homepage `siteMonitor` probes
#     against each app's public URL (probe-based; deliberately NO docker socket —
#     on the VPS it would only see VPS containers; observability.md HD-180 note).
#   - Domen · technical: tailnet-only admin dashboards (stats/logs/csui/sec/
#     traefik/auto/dsh/pi-dev + headscale control plane). Hidden from the family
#     group by `homepage_show_technical` (default true). Grafana (stats) is
#     Domen's technical dashboard — never a family tile.
#   - Soon: deploy-gated apps (Phase 3/4 hosts not provisioned yet) rendered as
#     description-only tiles (href '#') so the family sees the roadmap without
#     dead links; gated by `homepage_show_soon` (default true).
#
# Probe policy: siteMonitor is used ONLY for FQDNs the homepage container can
# actually resolve+reach (public CNAMEs). Tailnet-only names (stats/logs/csui/
# sec/traefik/auto/dsh/pi-dev/ai per HD-248) are NOT probed — the homepage
# container is not a tailnet node and would render false-red dots. Their health
# plane is Grafana itself.

# HD-17: manual HA failover buttons (docs/smart-home-failover.md). href cards call
# the ha-failover-api endpoint on oldsrv (?token= GET; POST with X-Failover-Token
# also supported). Forward REQUIRES the HmIP-RFUSB stick physically moved to oldsrv.
# Gated (HD-217): rendered only when group_var homepage_failover_button is true -
# false until HD-17 goes live (Phase 4), so no dead buttons / undefined-var lookups.
{% if homepage_failover_button %}
- Smart Home Failover:
    - HA Forward Takeover:
        icon: sh-home-assistant
        href: "http://{{ failover_api_url }}/failover?token={{ lookup('community.general.onepassword', 'ha-failover_api', field='credential', vault=op_vault) }}"
        description: Pi → oldsrv (RMat → wait CCU → VIP → HA standby)
    - HA Reverse Failback:
        icon: sh-home-assistant
        href: "http://{{ failover_api_url }}/failback?token={{ lookup('community.general.onepassword', 'ha-failover_api', field='credential', vault=op_vault) }}"
        description: oldsrv → Pi (VIP back, standby off)
{% endif %}

